coded protein is highly conserved in vertebrate genomes but has no significant similarity to any other human protein. [provided by RefSeq, Dec 2019].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q96GV9","text":"Regulates the macrophage function, by enhancing the resolution of inflammation and wound repair functions mediated by M2 macrophages (PubMed:30659109). The regulation of macrophage function is, due at least in part, to its ability to inhibit glycolysis (PubMed:30659109). May also play a role in trafficking of proteins via its interaction with UNC119 and UNC119B cargo adapters: may help the release of UNC119 and UNC119B cargo or the recycling of UNC119 and UNC119B (PubMed:22085962). May play a role in ciliary membrane localization via its interaction with UNC119B and protein transport into photoreceptor cells (PubMed:22085962)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}